                        


Item #:  SCP-5913

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  Containment of SCP-5913 is a 16 x 60 ft (about 3.7 x 5.5m) room constructed out of tungsten, subject is to keep under the observer of the foundation surveillances at all times. All personnel are to test for cognitohazardous corruption before they entered its containment cell. All personnel of the foundation are advised to not make any kinds of physical interactions with the subject.

Description : SCP-5913 is a humanoid entity dressed up in a bartender suit of the 1920s, which consisted of wearing a white shirt, a black or red tie, black trousers, and black shoes, subject measures 6 to 14 feet tall has a general appearance as a tall black figure that has no human facial features of any kind; it shows very little muscle mass, arms are out of proportion with the rest of the body, the subject has shown to have no signs of hair, eyes, nose, its mouth can open up to two (2) times the norm of a normal human, and has normal-looking bare hands, albeit with fingers longer and bonier than a typical human approximately 1.5 meters each. However, it is possible that this is not SCP-5913’s real form, and that it is actually an eldritch being whose true form cannot be comprehended.

SCP-5913 is capable of speech and understands normal human languages, however, its speech is hard to be understand by normal peoples, the subject seems to have different respiratory sounds which cause it to have issues in speaking.

Attempting to kill SCP-5913 often has some major problems because of its significant physical and anomalous abilities. It has always observed to have high strength, speed, and reflexes. Documented speed has varied from three-thousand and eighty-seven kilometers per hour (3087km/h), however, the subject prefers to teleport rather than running because of exhausted, other than that the subject is not invulnerable it can still be injure, although the subject has shown to have remarkable ability to ignore pain, shock, and have a strong regenerative healing factor that could help it recovered from injured wounds on it’s the body.1

The tendrils that sprout from SCP-5913’s body can grab, and attack, other than that it can also use the tendrils as a shield to protect the entity away from harm2

Documents of SCP-5913 anomalous abilities have also shown that certain contemporary views see its movement as unlimited as if it can move its body. It is rarely seen to move and goes from standing still to teleporting within the blink of an eye. There is no apparent coherency to SCP-5913’s movements or position, and it can teleport several dozen times to various locations in a few seconds. SCP-5913 does not flee and can be just as dangerous standing still as when teleporting. SCP-5913 capable of – and often will – stay within several dozen feet of its target, no matter how they try to escape. This seems to be part of SCP-5913 psychological attack to stay just within visual range without attacking — the fact that it is there, no matter what, it described as worse than being attacked, the psychological effects often deteriorating the mind of the person.

SCP-5913 appears to follow all targets regardless of where they go, or where and how they hide. It isn’t certain how it does this, but it seems to be able to keep a perfect trace on its targets. These accounts vary from person to person, but being a target of SCP-5913 is almost contagious or memetic. One can become its victim by encountering someone it is already targeting. Basic research and even collecting information doesn’t appear to incur its notice. A theory sprouts from this, discussing how it could be able to track several people at once, due to the apparent number of people invested. This theory states he is an omnipresent being.

The skin of the subject can inflict diseases upon those who touch it, any humans who come in contact with the subject’s skin would cause them to suffer some common diseases.3
